  {"t": "Three levels, one name", "b": "Every table is catalog.schema.table inside a metastore. Catalogs and schemas are containers; tables, views, volumes and functions live inside them. Layers such as bronze, silver and gold are usually schemas or catalogs."},
  {"t": "Managed or external: who owns the files", "b": "Unity Catalog manages a managed table's files in the catalog's or schema's storage, optimises them (predictive optimization) and deletes them after DROP TABLE, once the recovery period ends (7 days by default; UNDROP brings a table back inside it). An external table points at a path under an external location; DROP TABLE removes only the definition and leaves the files. Databricks recommends managed tables unless other systems must read the files directly or the format is not Delta or Iceberg."},
  {"t": "Converting external to managed", "b": "ALTER TABLE ... SET MANAGED copies the data and log into managed storage, with only a minute or two of blocked writes at the end. It needs a Delta table, table ownership, and Databricks Runtime 17.3 LTS or serverless. The old files are kept for 14 days, and UNSET MANAGED rolls back within that window."},
  {"t": "Privileges flow down", "b": "A privilege on a catalog applies to every schema and table in it, including future ones; a privilege on a schema applies to its tables. To read a table a user needs three things: USE CATALOG on the catalog, USE SCHEMA on the schema and SELECT on the table (or on a parent). MODIFY allows writes, CREATE TABLE allows new tables in a schema, and BROWSE lets people see that objects exist without reading them."},
  {"t": "Who can grant", "b": "The object's owner (the creator, at first), the owner of its catalog or schema, a metastore admin, or anyone holding MANAGE on the object. MANAGE lets someone grant, revoke and drop without owning the object, and several principals can hold it. Grant to groups rather than people, so access follows team changes."},
  {"t": "There is no DENY statement", "b": "Unity Catalog grants are additive: you remove access with REVOKE, and a user keeps whatever another grant or group still gives them. The legacy Hive metastore table ACLs had DENY; Unity Catalog does not. The only deny in Unity Catalog is the ABAC DENY policy (Beta), which today covers only the MANAGE ACCESS CONTROL privilege and overrides every grant."},
  {"t": "Row filters and column masks", "b": "Both are SQL functions attached to one table. A row filter returns true for rows a user may see; a column mask returns the real value or a masked one. Inside them, is_account_group_member('group') checks who is asking. The table owner or a holder of MANAGE attaches them. One mask per column, and filters and masks cannot be put on a view."},
  {"t": "ABAC: one policy, many tables", "b": "Governed tags are defined once for the account (for example pii = ssn). Tag columns and tables, then write a policy on a catalog or schema: TO which principals, EXCEPT whom, which tagged columns to mask or which rows to filter. New tables that get the tag are covered automatically, and table owners cannot override the policy. Needs Databricks Runtime 16.4 or serverless."},
